  "description": "Read the Monero blockchain from a workflow: look up a transaction or a block, watch what is moving and what is waiting to confirm, and see the network's hash rate, its fees and the total coin supply. It can also answer the two questions Monero's privacy otherwise makes hard: whether a payment to your address has arrived, and proof to a recipient that you paid them. Amounts come back in XMR, times in UTC, and an encrypted amount is reported as encrypted rather than as zero. No account or API key is required. Disclaimer: this is an independent integration with the community-run Onion Monero Blockchain Explorer and its public instance at xmrchain.net; it is not affiliated with, endorsed by, or sponsored by the Monero Project.",
  "display_name": "Monero Explorer",
  "id": "monero_explorer"
}
